[{"answer":"So, Rosie and Martin,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-14-test-2-part-3-2023-01-29-21-16-46/1.mp3"},{"answer":"let's look at what you've got for your presentation on woolly mammoths.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-14-test-2-part-3-2023-01-29-21-16-46/2.mp3"},{"answer":"OK, we've got a short outline here.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-14-test-2-part-3-2023-01-29-21-16-46/3.mp3"},{"answer":"Thanks.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-14-test-2-part-3-2023-01-29-21-16-46/4.mp3"},{"answer":"So it's about a research project in North America?","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-14-test-2-part-3-2023-01-29-21-16-46/5.mp3"},{"answer":"Yes.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-14-test-2-part-3-2023-01-29-21-16-46/6.mp3"},{"answer":"But we thought we needed something general about woolly mammoths in our introduction,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-14-test-2-part-3-2023-01-29-21-16-46/7.mp3"},{"answer":"to establish that they were related to our modern elephant,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-14-test-2-part-3-2023-01-29-21-16-46/8.mp3"},{"answer":"and they lived thousands of years ago in the last ice age.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-14-test-2-part-3-2023-01-29-21-16-46/9.mp3"},{"answer":"Maybe we could show a video clip of a cartoon about mammoths.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-14-test-2-part-3-2023-01-29-21-16-46/10.mp3"},{"answer":"But that'd be a bit childish.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-14-test-2-part-3-2023-01-29-21-16-46/11.mp3"},{"answer":"Or we could have a diagram,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-14-test-2-part-3-2023-01-29-21-16-46/12.mp3"},{"answer":"it could be a timeline to show when they lived, with illustrations?","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-14-test-2-part-3-2023-01-29-21-16-46/13.mp3"},{"answer":"Or we could just show a drawing of them walking in the ice?","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-14-test-2-part-3-2023-01-29-21-16-46/14-2024-11-06-20-10-22.mp3"},{"answer":"No, let's go with your last suggestion.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-14-test-2-part-3-2023-01-29-21-16-46/15.mp3"},{"answer":"Good.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-14-test-2-part-3-2023-01-29-21-16-46/16.mp3"},{"answer":"Then you're describing the discovery of the mammoth tooth on St Paul's Island in Alaska,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-14-test-2-part-3-2023-01-29-21-16-46/17.mp3"},{"answer":"and why it was significant.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-14-test-2-part-3-2023-01-29-21-16-46/18.mp3"},{"answer":"Yes.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-14-test-2-part-3-2023-01-29-21-16-46/19.mp3"},{"answer":"The tooth was found by a man called Russell Graham.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-14-test-2-part-3-2023-01-29-21-16-46/20.mp3"},{"answer":"He picked it up from under a rock in a cave.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-14-test-2-part-3-2023-01-29-21-16-46/21.mp3"},{"answer":"He knew it was special -","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-14-test-2-part-3-2023-01-29-21-16-46/22.mp3"},{"answer":"for a start it was in really good condition,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-14-test-2-part-3-2023-01-29-21-16-46/23.mp3"},{"answer":"as if it had been just extracted from the animal's jawbone.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-14-test-2-part-3-2023-01-29-21-16-46/24.mp3"},{"answer":"Anyway, they found it was 6,500 years old.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-14-test-2-part-3-2023-01-29-21-16-46/25.mp3"},{"answer":"So why was that significant?","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-14-test-2-part-3-2023-01-29-21-16-46/26.mp3"},{"answer":"Well the mammoth bones previously found on the North American mainland were much less recent than that.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-14-test-2-part-3-2023-01-29-21-16-46/27.mp3"},{"answer":"So this was really amazing.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-14-test-2-part-3-2023-01-29-21-16-46/28.mp3"},{"answer":"Then we're making an animated diagram to show the geography of the area in prehistoric times.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-14-test-2-part-3-2023-01-29-21-16-46/29.mp3"},{"answer":"So originally, St Paul's Island wasn't an island,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-14-test-2-part-3-2023-01-29-21-16-46/30.mp3"},{"answer":"it was connected to the mainland,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-14-test-2-part-3-2023-01-29-21-16-46/31.mp3"},{"answer":"and mammoths and other animals like bears were able to roam around the whole area.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-14-test-2-part-3-2023-01-29-21-16-46/32.mp3"},{"answer":"Then the climate warmed up and the sea level began to rise,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-14-test-2-part-3-2023-01-29-21-16-46/33.mp3"},{"answer":"and the island got cut off from the mainland.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-14-test-2-part-3-2023-01-29-21-16-46/34.mp3"},{"answer":"So those mammoths on the island couldn't escape;","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-14-test-2-part-3-2023-01-29-21-16-46/35.mp3"},{"answer":"they had to stay on the island.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-14-test-2-part-3-2023-01-29-21-16-46/36.mp3"},{"answer":"And in fact the species survived there for thousands of years","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-14-test-2-part-3-2023-01-29-21-16-46/37.mp3"},{"answer":"after they'd become extinct on the mainland.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-14-test-2-part-3-2023-01-29-21-16-46/38.mp3"},{"answer":"So why do you think they died out on the mainland?","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-14-test-2-part-3-2023-01-29-21-16-46/39.mp3"},{"answer":"No one's sure.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-14-test-2-part-3-2023-01-29-21-16-46/40.mp3"},{"answer":"Anyway, next we'll explain how Graham and his team identified the date when the mammoths became extinct on the island.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-14-test-2-part-3-2023-01-29-21-16-46/41.mp3"},{"answer":"They concluded that the extinction happened 5,600 years ago,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-14-test-2-part-3-2023-01-29-21-16-46/42.mp3"},{"answer":"which is a very precise time for a prehistoric extinction.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-14-test-2-part-3-2023-01-29-21-16-46/43.mp3"},{"answer":"It's based on samples they took from mud at the bottom of a lake on the island.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-14-test-2-part-3-2023-01-29-21-16-46/44.mp3"},{"answer":"They analysed it to find out what had fallen in over time -","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-14-test-2-part-3-2023-01-29-21-16-46/45.mp3"},{"answer":"bits of plants, volcanic ash and even DNA from the mammoths themselves.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-14-test-2-part-3-2023-01-29-21-16-46/46.mp3"},{"answer":"It's standard procedure, but it took nearly two years to do.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-14-test-2-part-3-2023-01-29-21-16-46/47.mp3"},{"answer":"So why don't you quickly go through the main sections of your presentation","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-14-test-2-part-3-2023-01-29-21-16-46/48.mp3"},{"answer":"and discuss what action's needed for each part?","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-14-test-2-part-3-2023-01-29-21-16-46/49.mp3"},{"answer":"OK.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-14-test-2-part-3-2023-01-29-21-16-46/50.mp3"},{"answer":"So for the introduction, we're using a visual,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-14-test-2-part-3-2023-01-29-21-16-46/51.mp3"},{"answer":"so once we've prepared that we're done.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-14-test-2-part-3-2023-01-29-21-16-46/52.mp3"},{"answer":"I'm not sure.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-14-test-2-part-3-2023-01-29-21-16-46/53.mp3"},{"answer":"I think we need to write down all the ideas we want to include here,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-14-test-2-part-3-2023-01-29-21-16-46/54.mp3"},{"answer":"not just rely on memory.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-14-test-2-part-3-2023-01-29-21-16-46/55.mp3"},{"answer":"How we begin the presentation is so important...","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-14-test-2-part-3-2023-01-29-21-16-46/56.mp3"},{"answer":"Umm, you're right.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-14-test-2-part-3-2023-01-29-21-16-46/57.mp3"},{"answer":"The discovery of the mammoth tooth is probably the most dramatic part,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-14-test-2-part-3-2023-01-29-21-16-46/58.mp3"},{"answer":"but we don't have that much information,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-14-test-2-part-3-2023-01-29-21-16-46/59.mp3"},{"answer":"only what we got from the online article.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-14-test-2-part-3-2023-01-29-21-16-46/60.mp3"},{"answer":"I thought maybe we could get in touch with the researcher who led the team","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-14-test-2-part-3-2023-01-29-21-16-46/61.mp3"},{"answer":"and ask him to tell us a bit more.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-14-test-2-part-3-2023-01-29-21-16-46/62.mp3"},{"answer":"Great idea.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-14-test-2-part-3-2023-01-29-21-16-46/63.mp3"},{"answer":"What about the section with the initial questions asked by the researchers?","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-14-test-2-part-3-2023-01-29-21-16-46/64.mp3"},{"answer":"We've got a lot on that but we need to make it interesting.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-14-test-2-part-3-2023-01-29-21-16-46/65.mp3"},{"answer":"We could ask the audience to suggest some questions about it","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-14-test-2-part-3-2023-01-29-21-16-46/66.mp3"},{"answer":"and then see how many of them we can answer.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-14-test-2-part-3-2023-01-29-21-16-46/67.mp3"},{"answer":"I don't think it would take too long.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-14-test-2-part-3-2023-01-29-21-16-46/68.mp3"},{"answer":"Yes that would add a bit of variety.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-14-test-2-part-3-2023-01-29-21-16-46/69.mp3"},{"answer":"Then the section on further research carried out on the island - analysing the mud in the lake.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-14-test-2-part-3-2023-01-29-21-16-46/70.mp3"},{"answer":"I wonder if we've actually got too much information here,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-14-test-2-part-3-2023-01-29-21-16-46/71.mp3"},{"answer":"should we cut some?","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-14-test-2-part-3-2023-01-29-21-16-46/72.mp3"},{"answer":"I don't think so,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-14-test-2-part-3-2023-01-29-21-16-46/73.mp3"},{"answer":"but it's all a bit muddled at present.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-14-test-2-part-3-2023-01-29-21-16-46/74.mp3"},{"answer":"Yes, maybe it would be better if it followed a chronological pattern.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-14-test-2-part-3-2023-01-29-21-16-46/75.mp3"},{"answer":"I think so.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-14-test-2-part-3-2023-01-29-21-16-46/76.mp3"},{"answer":"The findings and possible explanations section is just about ready,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-14-test-2-part-3-2023-01-29-21-16-46/77.mp3"},{"answer":"but we need to practice it so we're sure it won't overrun.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-14-test-2-part-3-2023-01-29-21-16-46/78.mp3"},{"answer":"I think it should be OK,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-14-test-2-part-3-2023-01-29-21-16-46/79.mp3"},{"answer":"but yes, let's make sure.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-14-test-2-part-3-2023-01-29-21-16-46/80.mp3"},{"answer":"In the last section, relevance to the present day,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-14-test-2-part-3-2023-01-29-21-16-46/81.mp3"},{"answer":"you've got some good ideas but...","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-14-test-2-part-3-2023-01-29-21-16-46/82.mp3"},{"answer":"this is where you need to move away from the ideas of others and give your own viewpoint.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-14-test-2-part-3-2023-01-29-21-16-46/83.mp3"},{"answer":"OK, we'll think about that.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-14-test-2-part-3-2023-01-29-21-16-46/84.mp3"},{"answer":"Now shall we...","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-14-test-2-part-3-2023-01-29-21-16-46/85.mp3"}]
